};
var b = a[Math.random() &gt; 0.5 ? &quot;f1&quot; : &quot;f2&quot;];
b.a &amp;&amp; b();

Note that a.f1 does not have a property defined on it anymore, though it still appears to be checked on this line of code:

b.a &amp;&amp; b();

