<issue>
make verify() possible if there is inlined different method call on other mock
To reproduce, run this as a test case:

	private static interface Foo {void setFoo(String bar);}
	private static interface Bar {String getBar();}

	@Test
	public void testVerifyFails() throws Exception {
		Foo foo = Mockito.mock(Foo.class);
		Bar bar = Mockito.mock(Bar.class);
		bar.getBar();
		verify(foo).setFoo(bar.getBar());
	}

The verify should fail, since setFoo(String) was never called, but it will
succeed.

I'm using 1.8 on Linux, JDK 1.6.

If you comment out the second-to-last line:
//              bar.getBar();
it will fail, complaining like this:
# Wanted but not invoked:
# bar.getBar();

So what seems to be happening is that the mock invocation of getBar(),
passed as the parameter to the setFoo(String) invocation, confuses verify()
into thinking that it should verify getBar(), rather than setFoo(String).

</issue>
